in one of the most burning  questions I personally have about the  story of Tears of the Kingdom hence I  thought it would be fun to go for some  of the history of Hyrule Sky  civilizations and see how they stack up  against the sky world scene in the  upcoming title I will skip locations  from entries that take place outside  Hyrule so no Triforce Heroes while it  does have its own realm in the sky  there's practically no backstory given  about this place and I highly doubt the  history of high Topia will have any  bearing on the events taking place in  tears of the Kingdom so sit back relax  and let us Venture into the clouds don't  forget your parachute though  while the majority of hyrule's  population has been living on the fields  mountains inside forests lakes and  rivers of the Kingdom since ancient  times there are those who have made a  home for themselves in and above the  clouds from Modest villages to  impressive Feats of engineering to  Majestic towers that pierce the heavens  according to their backstories most if  not all of them were built in the  unified timeline so before the timeline  split into three and have existed in the  skies above Hyrule ever since naturally  this raises questions like why didn't we  see any of these floating rocks and  buildings in games like say Ocarina of  Time well I mean we know why it's  because they hadn't thought of these  plot points yet back in 98. however  thanks to Skyward Sword we got an actual  in-universe explanation for it without  having to break the fourth wall it's not  because they are too high up or too  small to see though their altitude may  vary they seem to exist somewhere  between the low to mid-level Cloud layer  which in real life starts around 6500  feet or about two kilometers to put that  into perspective you can see commercial  airliner with the naked eye well above  25  000 feet or about seven and a half  kilometers so realistically speaking a  place like the Palace of winds with its  massive size should be visible to an  observer on ground level but it's not  the explanation given for this phenomena  is one that solves a lot of mysteries  and plot holes in the Zelda series magic  more specifically a magical barrier  which I've talked about plenty in other  videos an invisible border created  thousands of years before the events of  Skyward Sword by goddess hylia at the  end of Skyward Sword there's nothing  that indicates that this barrier has  ceased to exist no cutscene where it  dissipates or anything like that so  there's reason to believe that it's  still up there even after the countless  years that have passed since and breath  of the wild seems to corroborate this  while we don't know its exact placement  in the timeline the game is confirmed to  take place at the very end and here we  can see the dragons departing for the  skies through a vortex-like sky portal  very reminiscent of the Portal's link  creates and travels through in Skyward  Sword which in my opinion is solid proof  that there's still something in place  that separates Heaven and Earth as for  the inner workings of the barrier it's  not explained in great detail but we do  know a few things about it first and  foremost it does not act like a force  field stuff has been able to pass  through it unscathed and can even be  retrieved from the surface by link on  more than one occasion in fact the  father of one of the residents in  skyloft used an old robot he fixed up to  salvage goods from below the clouds long  before the portals were created the  reason why the people themselves don't  Venture below the clouds is because as  the game explains the Loft Wings do not  dare approach the cloud barrier and even  if they did the vast majority of  skyloft's residents have been taught to  believe that nothing exists below the  clouds in short the barrier seems to act  as a sort of one-way mirror as opposed  to a brick wall despite this people have  been aware of the existence of the Sky  Realm and throughout the centuries  civilizations have gained access to it  through various means either by  constructing enormous Towers like the  Tower of winds employ technology like  high-powered cannons to blast their way  up or utilizing powerful magic or  technology to lift their entire home up  into the clouds now before we move on I  have to make one important distinction  although the skies above Hyrule are  sometimes referred to as the heavens or  the Heavenly realm or something of that  nature it is not the heaven as in the  religious sense which is a bit confusing  but the actual Heaven which does in fact  exist in the Zelda Mythos is a place  we've never seen or visited before and  is where the gods are set to reside it's  basically on a completely different  plane of existence and in Ocarina of  Time It's explained that after the  world's creation this is where the three  golden goddesses departed to leaving the  Triforce behind at the point in space  where they cross Dimensions the  locations we'll be discussing today  still occupy the quote-unquote normal  World also referred to as the world of  Light which includes the kingdom of  Hyrule as well however it is implied  that the Sky Realm exists in close  proximity to the heavens and the gods  and is therefore considered to be one of  the most sacred places imaginable in  Shintoism which has been a big  inspiration for the Zelda mythology  since the 90s it is believed that there  exists a bridge that connects the  heavens and the the Earth known as the  ameno ukayashi The Floating Bridge of  Heaven which is believed to exist or  have existed high up in the sky  somewhere and is sometimes equated to a  rainbow another reoccurring theme in  Zelda most notably for today's subject  in four Swords Adventures where Zelda  uses her power to create a bridge in the  realm of the heavens as for the Heavenly  bridge and Shintoism some believe it  collapsed the earth and its remains  formed parts of Kyoto but others suggest  that it survived into modern times and  has remained invisible and intangible to  those who had not purified their hearts  unsurprisingly the idea of purity of  heart has often been equated with Hyrule  Sky Realm as well in Skyward Sword  purification and spiritual growth play a  central role in Minish capits also  declared on more than one occasion that  the world in the sky is only accessible  to those who are pure of heart and in  breath of the wild shamaya claims that  only good kids can see the kingdom in  the sky and the ancient dragons too are  only visible to pure-hearted individuals  which often includes young children it's  likely the main reason why so many  civilizations in Zelda have sought  access to the world above the clouds and  why only a select few succeeded in doing  so they wanted to be closer to their  gods and perhaps even establish some  sort of communication with them even in  games that don't take place in Hyrule we  can see similar attempts by Mortals to  reach the heavens a prime example being  the stone tower in Majora's Mask now for  the people of skyloft their Ascension  was out of pure necessity for the sake  of survival they were essentially  marooned on small outcrops of Hyrule  surface sent into the Sky by their  goddess and over the centuries they  adapted to the new living conditions  after the threat of demise was finally  gone they then relocated back to the  surface leaving their former home in the  sky behind and establishing the kingdom  of Hyrule as we know it just like the  barrier there's no indication that  skyloft and adjacent islands like the  Isle of songs were destroyed or  descended back to Earth by all accounts  they should still be up there waiting to  be rediscovered the only exception of  course being the Isle of the Goddess  which did return to the surface and  reconnected with the Temple of hylia the  massive statue which once towered over  skyloft can even be found inside breath  of the Wild's Forgotten Temple not only  that but it's the only place in Hyrule  where you can find actual depictions of  Loft Wings the very same depictions we  saw in Skyward Sword in fact the last  physical remnants of the world in the  sky found in the era of the wild or at  least that we know of the city in the  sky and the home of the wind tribe from  Minish Cap are a different story however  as opposed to a desperate Escape these  are civilizations who made a conscious  decision to leave the surface behind and  settle in the clouds the biggest  differences between the two are the  methods by which they achieved it and  the motivations behind their departure  the Oka are said to have constructed  their Sky City around the same time the  hylians first came into existence and  did so using highly advanced technology  the likes of which dwarfed any other  race or faction alive back then it's  worth mentioning that most of what we  know about this place and its people is  told to us from the Viewpoint of the  hylians and the hylians alone often  times in the form of old stories and  legends some of which contradict each  other or present more than one  possibility this because comes obvious  when talking to the Hylian researcher  Chad I mean Chad Chad implies that the  history of the aoka and their floating  Capital has been all but lost and are  only now being pieced together through  archaeological discoveries so basically  Shad is a Zelda theorist like me because  of this it's hard to paint an accurate  picture regarding the history and  timeline of the city in the sky and its  construction and localization  differences between the Japanese and  English versions of Twilight Princess  haven't exactly helped for example in  English Shad says that it's believed  that the Oka created the hylians which  is in stark contrast to the Japanese  text where he says that the Oka created  or established the land of Hyrule not  the Hylian people themselves the word  Oka is a western invention as well and  is an obvious play on the word cuckoo  hyrule's equivalent of chickens their  Japanese name is much more literal and  roughly translates to Sky person Sky  people or Sky being historically the  hylians are considered to be the God's  chosen people however the theory goes  that the Oka race was even closer to the  gods than the hylians were after their  departure from the surface the Oka  maintained contact with the kingdom of  Hyrule but only through one chosen  representative known as the messenger to  the heavens who would use an artifact  called the rod of the heavens and a book  capable of translating yoga alphabet  into the Hylian Language by the time of  Twilight Princess the two races have  long since been cut off from each other  and seized all Communications for  reasons unknown hence why knowledge  about the yoka faded into Legend as for  the fate of the city in the sky well we  have no idea the city and its  inhabitants have never been brought up  again in future titles not even in  Skyward Sword which came out five years  after the fact as such we don't know if  the city still exists though similar to  skyloft there's nothing that indicates  that it doesn't so presumably it too  might still be out there somewhere  hidden amongst the clouds  lastly we have the realm of the heavens  the only area to make an appearance in  more than one Zelda game three to be  exact Minish Cap four Swords and four  Swords Adventures it's a bit of a shame  that four Swords adventure's timeline  placement is so divisive because the  realm of the heavens is one of the most  historically Rich locations in the  series It's actually an umbrella term  which comprises three main areas the  Tower of winds the cloud tops and the  Palace of winds the latter of which is  present in all aforementioned titles  Minish Cap tells the story of a tribe  who is similar to the Oka elevated their  entire home into the heavens but as  opposed to Super advanced technology  they instead did so by mastering a  powerful type of magic referred to as  wind magic after they left for the skies  they too stayed in contact with the  hylians back on the surface and one of  the late Kings of Hyrule King Gustav is  said to have been very fond of them  unlike the Oka however the tribe did not  isolate themselves completely and did in  fact travel between their home in the  sky and the kingdom below you can even  spot two of them at the pakori festival  at the beginning of the game prior to  their Ascension they lived in and around  a place called The Fortress of winds  where they kept and watched over one of  four sacred Elements which would later  be obtained by link and used to create  the four sword only the base of the  Fortress remains back on earth and the  section they took into the sky with them  became known as the Palace of wind the  cloud tops is an area situated right  below the palace and is where in Minish  Cap most of the tribe hangs out and have  made a home for themselves it's a pretty  extensive area and as the name suggests  it's mostly just cloud formations with  the only significant architecture being  the tribe's home base the first game to  take place after Minish Gap the original  four Swords only features the Palace of  winds which in this game is called  vati's Palace after the main antagonist  from Minish Cap who also makes a return  here although we never see this  happening in game after vati Broke Free  from his prison he apparently took  control of the palace since it's the  only location we visit in four Swords  there's no appearance nor mention of the  tribe of winds so either vati killed  them when he took control of the area or  perhaps they had long since migrated  back to the surface with who knows in  four zones Adventures which according to  the official timeline takes place close  to the end of the chronology the Palace  of winds makes a return once again as do  the cloud tops though here it's been  renamed to the Dark Cloud due to its  corruption but it's essentially the same  place once again vati is back for a  third time making him the most featured  Zelda antagonist besides Ganon to date  and finally the Tower of winds is  introduced as a new addition and for the  first time the area that makes up the  palace Cloud tops and the upper portions  of the tower are united under a single  name the realm of the heavens seeing as  the tower didn't exist prior to four  Swords Adventures we have to assume that  it was constructed much later in order  to gain easy access to the Palace of  winds which in Minish Cap was extremely  difficult to get to and only reserved  for chosen individuals we don't know why  they wanted access to the Palace but  it's implied that the highlands were at  the Forefront of its construction  because the means to access the tower  under the protection of the most elite  Knights of Hyrule those who are hoping  to see a return of the Palace of winds  and tears of the Kingdom might be  pointed though because during the climax  of the game the two structures collapsed  in on themselves with the tribe of winds  gone and the wind Sorcerer of vati  destroyed the magic that sustained these  historic buildings dissipated and thus  they started to crumble and crash down  to earth granted these events only took  place in the child timeline so if you  want to be technical the Palace of winds  at least should still exist in the other  two branches but I'm not so sure if  Nintendo would bother with the  technicality like that and that covers  the most prominent locations and  civilizations that exist or have existed  in the sky there's one race I left out  so far that being the Minish or the  pcori if you prefer who are said to have  arrived from the sky but unfortunately  we know next to nothing about the world  they came from and haven't seen any of  it say for the inside of a house it's  also confirmed to exist in a separate  Dimension so technically it's not even  part of the Sky Realm above Hyrule so  for now there's not much to say about it  over the years many have made attempts  to find connections between these  different groups and it's admirable just  how meticulous fans have been in their  research but thus far there's no hard  proof that they share any connection  beyond the fact that each resides in the  skies above somewhere and because most  of the games take place ages apart from  each other it's difficult to pinpoint a  clear and comprehensive timeline for all  these buildings and the people who made  them as much as I like to believe that  the okra may have evolved from The Loft  wings or that the tribe of winds from  Minish Cap are related to either skyloft  or the Oka their backstories and the  timeline of events are either too  ambiguous or differ too much for me to  be convinced of an unequivocal  connection my personal belief is that  they are all separate civilizations each  with their own history and Origins and  who achieved a similar goal of accessing  the Sky Realm through different methods  and for their own personal reasons it  explains why each of these locations is  so different both in terms of  architecture and the way they are kept  suspended in the air and may explain why  the islands and tears of the kingdom are  also unlike anything we've seen in the  series so far whoever built them may  just be yet another disconnected group  who followed in the same footsteps as  the Oka and the tribe of winds people  who chose to leave the surface of Hyrule  in search of a higher purpose while  there's definitely something mystical  and spiritual about these islands  especially with all the shinto-like  structures and Lotus imagery at the same  time there's also hints of a  technology-based culture the man-made  spiers or antennas situated at the  bottom of the rock formations the  strange automata seen in the second  teaser we can even see what looks like a  cable running from one Island to the  next I guess even Sky people need a good  internet connection additionally one of  the antennas or spiers or whatever you  want to call them seems to emit a green  glow from its tip almost like a booster  engine of sorts which could be what's  keeping these islands afloat in that  sense the islands have more in common  with the okas methods of utilizing  technology than it does the more magical  approach as seen with the Palace of  winds and skyloft both of which didn't  require man-made factors to stay  suspended like propellers or boosters  one can also not help but draw parallels  with the sheikah and their technology  yet another group who were able to  elevate massive structures with their  engineering skills skills far beyond  that of the other medieval style races  in high rule the ancient blue energy  that fuels the sheikah technology shares  a lot of similarities with the new green  energy type introduced in tears of the  Kingdom both seem to act like a fuel can  give life to robots is used to conjure  up god-like abilities like time  manipulation and if we look at the logo  of Tears of the Kingdom apparently both  can take on the shape of an energy-based  weapon or lightsaber they're basically  lightsabers I'm not saying the two are  the same but they do exert similar  Behavior and the islands may have been  built on the same principle which if  true means that whoever inhabits or used  to inhabit them may have made similar  technological leaps as the Chica did one  aspect that sets the new islands apart  from any location covered so far is that  they are hinted to be part of a kingdom  we of course have the kingdom part in  the subtitle of the game which many have  suggested maybe referring to the world  in the sky and not the kingdom of Hyrule  but the existence of a so-called Sky  kingdom was actually foreshadowed by one  of the NPCs in breath of the wild none  of the previously mentioned locations  were ever referred to as a kingdom  skyloft was basically just a village  with barely any power structure the city  in the sky is well a city and the oh God  don't seem to have any royalty of their  own and while the wind tribe does have a  leader figure they are no Monarch by any  means now does that mean we won't see  skyloft or the city in the sky at all in  this game well no I mean technically  they have occupied the same space and as  I explained earlier there's no  indication that they cease to exist  after their respective stories in fact I  think it would be a huge missed  opportunity not to include at least one  of these areas perhaps as an abandoned  ruin or dare I say even a dungeon it  would be one of the greatest callbacks  to a pass Zelda location ever we already  saw remnants of the era of Skyward Sword  on the surface in breath of the wild so  if this stuff survived I see very little  reason why skyloft shouldn't have either  now there's one more place I haven't  covered so far which is referred to as a  kingdom on occasion and has some  resemblances to the islands in the sky  as well that being the sacred realm a  mystical place sometimes depicted as a  cluster of floating islands in what  looks like space I mean that's a planet  right there I initially wanted to  include the sacred realm as the fourth  area to talk about in regards to the  history of the Sky Realm however during  my research I came to realize just how  little we actually know and understand  about this place and how confusing and  contradictory the stories about it  really are on some occasions it's  described as a completely separate  Dimension that exists on its own which  means it could have very little to do  with the skies above Hyrule other times  Hyrule itself is referred to as the  sacred realm like in Twilight Princess  in A Link Between Worlds we actually  visit the sacred realm and even have  control over link brief as it may be and  it looks like just a place high up in  the cloud somewhere Zelda even says to  link that they are back home implying  they are back in Hyrule which moments  before Hilda said she would send them to  so is it a different dimension or just a  place in Hyrule somewhere up in the sky  perhaps like I said it's all very  confusing to say the least so instead of  tripling the runtime of this video I've  instead decided decided to make a  separate video dedicated entirely to the  sacred realm in the future so I hope you  look forward to that I'm also happy to  announce that I'll be working on another  tears of the Kingdom Theory which will  be a collaboration video with none other  than sir zeltic himself we don't have a  date scheduled just yet and we're still  bouncing ideas off each other but we're  aiming to get it done before we get new  footage of Tears of the Kingdom so  somewhere around mid to late January I  guess with that said thank you as always  for watching it wasn't much of a  Christmas themed video but happy  holidays either way and I hope you have  a great time celebrating a massive shout  out as always goes to my mods Discord  community and of course my members and  patreons you continue to make this  channel possible I hope to see you all  in the next video this is Dawn signing  off and have a good one  [Music]  foreign  [Music]  [Music]

